### Employee Management API - works with IntelliJ HTTP Client and VS Code REST Client
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@json = application/json

### ===================== SUCCESS SCENARIOS =====================

### 1. Create employee (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "department": "IT",
  "designation": "Software Engineer",
  "salary": 75000.00,
  "dateOfJoining": "2024-01-15"
}

### 1b. Create a second employee (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
  "phone": "9123456780",
  "department": "HR",
  "designation": "HR Manager",
  "salary": 82000.50,
  "dateOfJoining": "2023-06-01"
}

### 2. List all employees (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees

### 3. List with filters and sorting (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees?department=IT&status=ACTIVE&sortBy=salary&order=desc

### 4. Get employee by id (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/1

### 5. Full update (200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/1
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "department": "IT",
  "designation": "Senior Software Engineer",
  "salary": 95000.00,
  "dateOfJoining": "2024-01-15"
}

### 6. Deactivate employee (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/1/status
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "status": "INACTIVE" }

### 7. Reactivate employee (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/1/status
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "status": "ACTIVE" }

### 8. Search by keyword (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/search?keyword=john

### 9. List by department (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/department/IT

### 10. Stats (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/stats

### 11. Delete employee (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/2

### 12. Health check (bonus)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### ===================== FAILURE SCENARIOS =====================

### F1. Validation errors (400 with fieldErrors)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "firstName": "J",
  "lastName": "D0e",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "phone": "123",
  "department": "IT",
  "designation": "",
  "salary": -10,
  "dateOfJoining": "2999-01-01"
}

### F2. Duplicate email (409) - run request 1 twice
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "department": "IT",
  "designation": "Software Engineer",
  "salary": 75000.00,
  "dateOfJoining": "2024-01-15"
}

### F3. Invalid department enum in body (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "firstName": "Alan",
  "lastName": "Turing",
  "email": "alan@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543211",
  "department": "MARKETING",
  "designation": "Analyst",
  "salary": 50000,
  "dateOfJoining": "2024-01-15"
}

### F4. Salary above app.max-salary (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "firstName": "Rich",
  "lastName": "Person",
  "email": "rich@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543212",
  "department": "FINANCE",
  "designation": "CFO",
  "salary": 99999999,
  "dateOfJoining": "2024-01-15"
}

### F5. Get non-existent employee (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/9999

### F6. Update non-existent employee (404)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/9999
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "ghost@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "department": "IT",
  "designation": "Engineer",
  "salary": 70000,
  "dateOfJoining": "2024-01-15"
}

### F7. Update with another employee's email (409)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/1
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "department": "IT",
  "designation": "Engineer",
  "salary": 70000,
  "dateOfJoining": "2024-01-15"
}

### F8. Change status of non-existent employee (404)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/9999/status
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "status": "INACTIVE" }

### F9. Invalid status value (400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/1/status
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "status": "RETIRED" }

### F10. Delete non-existent employee (404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/9999

### F11. Unknown department path (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/department/MARKETING

### F12. Invalid sortBy (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees?sortBy=shoeSize

### F13. Non-numeric id (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/abc

### F14. Blank search keyword (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees/search?keyword=

### F15. Malformed JSON (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "firstName": "John",
